    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "The CLIPPER\nSIX MORE WINGS are being sported by PAA stewardesses as this second class of 1955 is graduated. L to r,\nfront row, Angie Natalie, Helen Blenke and Sally Taroncher; back row, Kathy Fabian, Judy Kittle and\nNila Lanier. The latter is a transfer from medical. (See picture below).\n6 More Are Graduated\nAt Stewardess School\nHalf a dozen more stewardesses were added to the Pan\nAmerican roster during June and a class of eight immediately\nbegan training at the COB flight service training school.\nHanded their wings after three\nJudith Louise Kittle, Cham-\npaigne, Ill; Kathleen\nEgg Harbor, N. J.; Sally\nHelen Catherine Blenke,\nAngelina Connie Na-\ntalie, Miami; and Nila V. Lanier,\nThe girls who launched the third\nsuccessive class of 1955 were:\nCarol Salter, Compton, Cal.; Sue\nMcLaughlin,\nDelray\nBeach,\nEleanor\nJarck,\nNew York\nFa.;\nCity;\nAnela\nAngeletti, Pompano Beach,\nFla.; Jane\nRieman,\nMiami; Mar-\njorie Peet, Hollywood\nFla.;\nVir-\nginia Loepp, Sioux City, Iowa; and\nAudrey Shurer, cargo employe at\nCOB\nFlight Service Superintendent\nDanny Gonzalez presented the girls\nwith their\nwings after graduation\nexercises at the flight service train-\ning school at COB\nIn the group will be the second\nconsecutive company employe who\nhas transferred into fight service.\nMiss Lanier, a nurse in the PAF\nmedical\noffice,\nJoins\nformer\nac-\ncounting files clerk Barbara\nSand-\ners\nwho was graduated\nwith the\npreceding class.\n1956 from Stewardess to Purser\nready to greet passengers\n1957 Canton Island in the Pacific\nNikki wins the wheel pool with #4\nchalked on the wheel having landed\nclosest to the Ground.",
      "Los Chavales de Espana Orchestra\nflying PAN AM from NYC to San Juan,\nPuerto Rico and Featuring American\nFlamenco Dancer Trini Reyes who strikes\na pose in the Airplane's Galley.\nThe other Photo's include the young son\nof one of the musicians sitting with the\nPurser, Nikki Jester. Stewardess on board\nis Miss Iris Frankel.",
      "1969 Nikki Jester attends first meeting of WWI and joins the MIA Chapter at\nthe Miami Springs Villas main building in a banquet room.\nDr. Sheffey from the Miami Children's Center was present and she gave a\npresentation on the Chapter's Charity.\nThis building was the home of Glenn Hammond Curtis, founder of Miami\nSprings, Hialeah and Opa Lock, FL. The room mentioned as a banquet room was\noriginally Mr. Curtiss' garage.\nPHOTO:\nSeated L to R Doris Pope, Doris Kinsel, Dr. Sheffy, Jane Galpin - President,\nRuth Francis and June\nStanding L to R Mac Paris, Fran Rinker, Harriet Mann, Mary Frantz, Kitty\nStickland, Aida Acle, Nikki Jester, Nancy Deem, Berit Fournier, Ann Thayer,\nMoncita Mc Naughton, Gloria Taylor, Berenice Demos and Sarita Lada",
      "MIAMI\nAFF"
    ],
